{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChB2EavWaBTp48dso5qTh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 14 is done and committed. Lint, typecheck, `npm run test:ts` (1904 assertions), `go build ./...` and `npm test` all pass. Every checklist item has real tests.\n\n**What I built** (all in `src/llm/`):\n- **The loop:** `agent.ts` holds the agent loop (`runConversation` plus the default constants). The decision about each model response lives in `review.ts` as a pure function.\n- **Supporting modules:** the ledger (`ledger.ts`), the work deadline (`deadline.ts`), final-argument checks with big integers kept exact (`final-args.ts`), step retries (`retry.ts`) and transcript size (`messages.ts`).\n- **Errors:** `errors.ts` gains `cutoffError`, which keeps the cause out of the matchable chain, and `FinalArgumentsError`. `details.stopCause` is now one of a fixed set of kinds, so tests never match message text.\n- **`createClient`** in `client.ts` wraps ticket 13's `ModelClient` into the `Client` the finder and verifier will call, and `usage()` returns the snake_case record shape.\n\n**Tests:** most tests drive the loop through a scripted fake `ModelClient` (`test/llm/agent-helpers.ts`). The HTTP items run against the real chat adapter and the fake inference server. The ledger has its own unit tests.\n\n**Things that differ from what you might expect:**\n- **Test order:** only the ledger went strictly test-first. I wrote the loop from spec 07 and the Go `agent.go`, then added tests per checklist item. To make sure those tests aren't just confirming the code, I broke the implementation on purpose in about a dozen places, one change at a time. All but one break failed a test. The exception is clearing a stale schema error after a rejected submission: in this design that error always stops the loop anyway, so clearing it can't change any result.\n- **No debug tracing:** the spec asks for `DEBUG=roast:*` tracing, but AGENTS.md says no `src/` module may import `@substrate-system/debug` until it passes the license check. It's noted for later.\n- **Request timeout:** ticket 13's client already enforces it, so the loop only combines the caller's signal with the deadline. The \"buffered tool call before a request timeout\" check runs over HTTP, with a server that sends one tool-call chunk and then stalls.\n- **Live tests:** I added `npm run test:live` and two DeepSeek tests. I had no API key, so I've only seen them skip; the live path itself has never run.\n- **No second JSON encoder:** following the ticket, I didn't add the spec's `goJsonStringify`, and tool results go through `encodeToolResult`. As a result, a `bigint` in an exploration tool's result comes back as `{\"error\": ...}` rather than as digits.\n\n**Two other changes:**\n- **Test helper fix:** `AbortSignal.timeout` timers don't keep Node running. A fake step that waits for an abort has to hold a timer of its own, or the test process just exits. The `aborted()` helper handles this.\n- **Docs and notes:** AGENTS.md has new notes on the loop's conventions and this test gotcha. Ticket-specific notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which isn't committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":222956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1521},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79353e88-0eda-49f3-aae4-5b092ab34fc4","uuid":"89918c92-d36c-4135-8f4a-49a39aa3cb48","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:26:39.013Z","request_id":"req_011ChB2EaYCSQSFLRMwBo1qn"}
